<h2 id="sec-2">How We Evaluated</h2>
<p>We cooked identical batches of french fries, chicken wings, and roasted vegetables in each air fryer, scoring on crispness and browning, capacity utilization, preheat time, noise level, control intuitiveness, cleanability, and footprint.</p>
<h2 id="sec-3">Detailed Reviews</h2>
<h3>1. Ninja Foodi Personal — Best Overall</h3>
<p>The Ninja Foodi Personal is a powerhouse in a compact package. Its 1,050-watt heating element and Rapid Air Technology produce restaurant-quality crispiness. The 1.5-quart ceramic-coated basket is perfect for 1-2 servings. At 11.8 x 10.2 x 12.6 inches, it fits comfortably on most counters.</p>
<div style="background:#F7F4EF;border-left:3px solid #C9A962;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-size:0.95rem"><strong>Best for:</strong> Singles, couples, and small households who want premium results in a compact footprint.</p></div>
<h3>2. COSORI 2-Qt — Best Value</h3>
<p>At $60, the COSORI 2-Quart delivers exceptional performance. The square basket design maximizes cooking space. Six one-touch presets handle everything from french fries to fish. The shake reminder beeps halfway through cooking.</p>
<h3>3. Philips XXL Premium — Best Premium Compact</h3>
<p>The Philips XXL Premium represents the premium end. TrueFry technology with Twin TurboStar ensures even air circulation. The digital touch interface is intuitive with 10 preset programs.</p>
<h2 id="sec-4">Size Guide</h2>
<ul><li><strong>1-1.5 quarts:</strong> Ideal for 1 person</li><li><strong>2 quarts:</strong> Best for couples or small families</li><li><strong>3+ quarts:</strong> Suitable for families of 3-4</li></ul>
<h2 id="sec-5">FAQs</h2>
<h3>Can I cook a full meal in a compact air fryer?</h3>
<p>Yes, but you'll need to cook in batches for families of 3 or more. A 2-quart model serves 2 people comfortably.</p>
<h3>Are compact air fryers safe?</h3>
<p>Absolutely. Air fryers are safer than deep frying with no hot oil splatters. Most models auto-shutoff when the basket is removed.</p>
<h2 id="sec-6">Final Verdict</h2>
<div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1A1A1A 0%,#2A2A2A 100%);color:white;padding:2rem;border-radius:12px;margin-top:2rem"><p style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 0.75rem 0;color:#C9A962">Our Recommendation</p><p style="margin:0;line-height:1.8">The <strong>Ninja Foodi Personal</strong> at $90 is the best compact air fryer. For budget buyers, the <strong>COSORI 2-Qt</strong> at $60 offers remarkable value. Those willing to invest more should consider the <strong>Philips XXL Premium</strong>.</p></div>
